※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 7011 LANG_MACRO_UNKNOWN

※ The lifting marks after a name invoke a macro, and where none of that name is
※ defined there is nothing to hand what is between them to.  A function is called
※ with parentheses, since what a function is handed is worked out first.

macro twice:
    ⌜$x⌝ → ⌜$x + $x⌝

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕narrow(thrice⌜1u8⌝, ⌜u6⌝) ?? 1u6
